le who believe that this uh  withdrawal was a mess that it was badly  planned that it was clumsy will they be  convinced by the reasoning that biden  just delivered  uh no if you if you don't think that joe  biden did a good job on this you're not  going to be convinced you're not going  to sit and listen  uh in a measured way and think that the  president delivered a recent argument  simply because  politics in america is now  very polarized and it's rare that  someone can be converted over to a  thinking the other way by a reasoned or  well put together constructive argument  and that will certainly be the case here  this is really joe biden  saying to those who may be undecided  look  it's better to be out of afghanistan  than in it's cheaper to be out of  afghanistan than in it is safer for  american service men and women to be out  of afghanistan rather than in and at  some point the decision had to be made  given a deal was already done and he  made reference to that deal that the  trump administration uh had done with  the taliban who said look there was a  deal done and this is true there was a  deal done with the taliban that said we  will pull the american troops out by  this date and that was may the 31st but  there was nothing in that deal that said  the taliban by that date had to be  involved in a coalition government with  the the existing afghan government or a  government of national unity there was  no term put to the taliban that if you  if we do this then you must do that  and he believes that that was a failing  in the deal and that is something that  republicans who have been attacking joe  biden over the last few weeks have  conspicuously failed uh to mention so  joe biden believes that what he did  he did with the best intentions and in  the circumstances that were presented to  him as he walked into the oval office on  january the 20th alan fisher they're  joining us with the very latest live  from the white house after off the back  of that